<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Amrel half year shr jumps, outlook fair.</title>
<headline>Amrel half year shr jumps, outlook fair.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     40	    vs 10</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs  -</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   12.61	 vs 2.99</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   19.88	 vs 3.98</p>
<p>    Tax			 7.14	  vs 0.84</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   25.63	 vs 29.94</p>
<p>    Turnover		  470.49	vs 442.58</p>
<p>Full name: Amalgamated Retail Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said its policy was to pay one dividend at the year-end.</p>
<p>Amrel said trading conditions remained tough but lower average borrowings had cut interest costs. This, together with the disposal of the loss-making footwear and apparel operations in the prior year, helped boost earnings.</p>
<p>The company said its renewed focus of the core furniture business and a drive to improve efficiencies were expected to reap benefits in the medium term. A satisfcatory growth in earnings was expected for the year as a whole.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
